\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {III}{\ignorespaces Bayesian comparison with parameterized GR-contamination degradation. SSFSR = standard single-field slow-roll inflation. The ``BF vs.\ Tuned'' column reports the Bayes factor against a tuned multifield competitor with \emph  {narrow} prior $[-5,+5]$ at the delta bounce prior; the corresponding broad $[-15,+15]$ multifield competitor gives BF~$\sim 17$ at $\sigma _{\rm  GR}=0.5$ (Table~\ref {tab:bayes} row~5), consistent with the narrow$\to $broad sweep BF~$\sim 7\to 17$ at the delta bounce prior reported in the prose of \S  \ref {sec:bayesian}. The bounce-vs-inflation comparison survives all treatment scenarios. $^a$The ``Corrected (10\% residual)'' row is, by construction, equal to ``Ideal'' at this template-overlap order: a 10\% residual GR contamination after correction has negligible impact on the Bayes factor at the reported significant-figure level ($\Delta \text  {BF} < 0.1$). It is included as a no-op sanity row, not as an independent configuration, and the two rows are not independent scenarios but rather bookend the same GR-free regime.}}{14}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:gr}{{III}{14}{Bayesian comparison with parameterized GR-contamination degradation. SSFSR = standard single-field slow-roll inflation. The ``BF vs.\ Tuned'' column reports the Bayes factor against a tuned multifield competitor with \emph {narrow} prior $[-5,+5]$ at the delta bounce prior; the corresponding broad $[-15,+15]$ multifield competitor gives BF~$\sim 17$ at $\sigma _{\rm GR}=0.5$ (Table~\ref {tab:bayes} row~5), consistent with the narrow$\to $broad sweep BF~$\sim 7\to 17$ at the delta bounce prior reported in the prose of \S \ref {sec:bayesian}. The bounce-vs-inflation comparison survives all treatment scenarios. $^a$The ``Corrected (10\% residual)'' row is, by construction, equal to ``Ideal'' at this template-overlap order: a 10\% residual GR contamination after correction has negligible impact on the Bayes factor at the reported significant-figure level ($\Delta \text {BF} < 0.1$). It is included as a no-op sanity row, not as an independent configuration, and the two rows are not independent scenarios but rather bookend the same GR-free regime}{table.3}{}}
